Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Description", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.958726074421812*^9, 
  3.958726078135477*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e9135187-42de-fe4e-ae09-\
d5868204815e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["This is one of four Mathematica notebooks created by Luk\[AAcute]\
\[SHacek] Polcar that form the supplemental material to the 2025 paper \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]name of the paper\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] by Luk\
\[AAcute]\[SHacek] Polcar and Vojt\[EHacek]ch Witzany.\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "This notebook consists of two parts:\n\nThe first part was authored by \
Andrew Spiers and is based on the publicly available notebook by Alfonso Garc\
\[IAcute]a-Parrado G\[OAcute]mez-Lobo. It sets up the Newman\[Dash]Penrose \
(NP) and Geroch\[Dash]Held\[Dash]Penrose (GHP) formalism and computes \
perturbed NP scalars. If this part is used in related research, please cite \
the following sources:\n\nA. Spiers, A. Pound, and J. Moxon, Second-order \
Teukolsky formalism in Kerr spacetime: formulation and nonlinear source, \
2023. https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevD.108.064002\n\nA. \
Garc\[IAcute]a-Parrado G\[OAcute]mez-Lobo, The N.P. and G.H.P. formalisms, \
2009. Available at: http://www.xact.es/Documentation/English/PublicNPGHP.nb\n\
\nThe second part was created by Luk\[AAcute]\[SHacek] Polcar and constructs \
the effective source for the modified Teukolsky equation localized on the \
matter shell. This source is built from the reconstructed (0,1) metric using \
the Hertz potential, with calculations carried out abstractly in the NP/GHP \
formalism. Finally, the source is decomposed into spin-weighted spherical \
harmonics. This part corresponds to Section IV of the paper."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9587260832229595`*^9, 3.958726083655905*^9}, {
   3.9587361696859035`*^9, 3.958736198406782*^9}, 
   3.958736285363781*^9},ExpressionUUID->"06bae936-7546-1243-92dd-\
acfe78281f14"]
}, Open  ]],

